jobs.description:
The Chief Technology Officer (CTO) is the highest-ranking technology leader in the organization, holding overall responsibility for the company's technology strategy, technical architecture, R&D systems, engineering organization, and technological innovation.

This role is responsible for translating business strategy into a long-term technology roadmap and supporting product innovation, business growth, and organizational scaling by building stable, scalable, secure, and efficient technology infrastructure and R&D systems.

Core Responsibilities

I. Technology Strategy
Formulate the company's medium- to long-term technology strategy and technology development roadmap;
Ensure alignment between technology strategy and overall corporate business strategy;
Evaluate emerging technologies and their commercial value;
Determine priorities for technology investment and R&D;
Provide strategic technology advice to the CEO, the Board of Directors, and senior management.

II. Technical Architecture and Platforms
Oversee the design and evolution of the enterprise's overall technical architecture;
Build stable, scalable, and high-performance technology platforms;
Establish standards for technical architecture and engineering practices;
Drive the development of capabilities in cloud computing, data platforms, AI, and automation;
Ensure technology infrastructure supports the company's long-term growth and scalability.

III. R&D and Engineering Management
Lead software engineering, R&D, and technical teams;
Establish efficient R&D processes and engineering management systems;
Set standards for R&D quality, delivery, and productivity;
Optimize product development and technology delivery workflows;
Promote Agile development, DevOps, and continuous delivery practices.

IV. Product-Technology Collaboration
Collaborate with product, design, and business teams to define product technology roadmaps;
Translate business requirements into technical solutions;
Assess the technical feasibility and development costs of product features;
Balance technical debt, investment in innovation, and business delivery requirements;
Ensure technical teams remain aligned with product strategy.

V. Technological Innovation
Establish a corporate system for technological innovation;
Evaluate AI, machine learning, automation, cloud computing, and other emerging technologies;
Drive the application of new technologies in products and operations;
Organize technical research, proof-of-concept (PoC) initiatives, and innovation projects;
Establish mechanisms to translate technological innovations into practical outcomes.

VI. Data and Artificial Intelligence
Formulate strategies for enterprise data and AI technology development;
Build data infrastructure and data governance frameworks;
Drive the application of machine learning, generative AI, and intelligent automation;
Ensure data quality, security, and availability;
Transform data capabilities into competitive advantages for products and the business.

VII. Information Security and Technology Risk
Establish an enterprise-wide technology security and risk management framework;
Oversee application, infrastructure, and data security;
Implement mechanisms for vulnerability management, disaster recovery, and business continuity;
Collaborate with security, legal, and compliance teams;
Oversee major technology risks and security incidents.

VIII. Technology Team and Organizational Development
Build a global, high-performance technology organization;
Manage technology teams including VP of Engineering, Engineering Directors, Architecture, Data, and AI;
Oversee the recruitment and development of senior technical talent;
Establish a technical talent pipeline and succession plan;
Foster an engineering culture and a technical leadership framework.

IX. Technology Budget and Resource Management
Formulate annual technology and R&D budgets;
Manage resources related to personnel, infrastructure, software, and vendors;
Optimize the technology investment portfolio;
Balance R&D investment with business value;
Enhance the return on investment (ROI) for technology.

Qualifications

Education
Bachelor’s degree or higher in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Information Technology, Electronic Engineering, or a related field;
Master’s degree, MBA, or advanced degree in Computer Science or Engineering preferred.

Work Experience
20+ years of experience in technology, engineering, R&D, or software development;
15+ years of senior technology leadership experience;
Experience in senior roles such as CTO, VP of Engineering, SVP of Engineering, or Chief Architect preferred;
Comprehensive experience spanning technology team building to enterprise-scale operations;
Experience managing global technology teams preferred.

Core Competencies
Enterprise technology strategy;
Technology architecture design;
Software engineering management;
Product-technology collaboration;
AI and data strategy;
Cloud computing and infrastructure;
Network and information security;
Technological innovation;
R&D organizational development;
Technology budget management;
Senior talent leadership;
Technology commercialization capability.

Key Performance Indicators (KPIs)
Product and technology delivery efficiency;
System stability and availability;
Product release cycles;
On-time completion rate of technology projects;
System performance and scalability;
Technology cost efficiency;
Engineering team productivity;
Reduction rate of technical debt;
Security incident and risk control;
Outcomes of technological innovation projects;
Technology ROI.

